sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: One voice turn on the phone
    accDescr: The wake word opens a Gemini Live session; on-device end-of-turn detection decides when the person has finished; a question for the engine goes through a small sub-agent over /mcp, its card is drawn on the phone, and the answer goes back to Gemini, which speaks it.
    %% Sources: app/.../service/WakeWordEngine.kt, WakeTwoStageDetector, AriaForegroundService.kt,
    %% LiveSessionController.kt, GeminiLiveSession.kt, turn/TurnTaker.kt, turn/EndOfTurnPolicy.kt,
    %% service/LiveToolbox.kt, service/AskEngine.kt, backend/engine/EngineMcpClient.kt,
    %% assistant/cards/ServerCards.kt; server/engine_mcp/views.py, server.py, tools.py, cards.py.
    actor person as Person
    participant wake as Wake word: VAD, keyword spotter, Vosk check
    participant turn as End of turn: Silero VAD + Smart Turn
    participant live as GeminiLiveSession: mic and speaker
    participant gemini as Gemini Live
    participant tools as LiveSessionController + LiveToolbox
    participant ask as ask_engine sub-agent (Gemini REST)
    participant engine as Engine /mcp tool registry
    participant screen as Assistant strip (cards)

    person->>wake: "Hey Alfred"
    wake->>live: start a conversation
    live->>gemini: WebSocket, household key, setup
    person->>live: speaks
    live->>turn: 32 ms audio windows
    turn->>gemini: activityStart, audio, activityEnd
    Note over turn: Smart Turn can only extend a turn, never end it early
    gemini-->>live: toolCall ask_engine
    live->>tools: run the tool ("Working...")
    tools->>ask: the question
    ask->>engine: tools/list, then tools/call
    engine->>engine: write fence, table fence, schema, handler
    engine-->>ask: text, card in _meta
    ask-->>screen: card (an unknown kind draws nothing)
    ask-->>tools: answer in words
    tools->>gemini: toolResponse
    gemini-->>live: spoken audio
    live-->>person: plays the answer
